{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "prompt",
            "if": "Edit(**/.claude/hooks/**)",
            "prompt": "You guard a project against re-creating assets that the installed aidd plugin already provides. Hook input: $ARGUMENTS\n\nIf tool_input.file_path is not inside a .claude/hooks, .claude/skills, .claude/commands, .claude/rules, or .claude/agents directory, respond {\"ok\": true}.\nOtherwise read tool_input.content and decide whether the new asset's role substantially overlaps one of these aidd assets:\n- command aidd:adr: アーキテクチャ決定記録 (ADR) を作成し docs/adr/ に保存する\n- command aidd:asset-audit: 利用側プロジェクトの .claude/ と CLAUDE.md を棚卸しし、削除・改訂・修正の候補を出す\n- command aidd:autonomous-review: 異種AIレビュー・根拠検証・品質ゲートを統合し、ローカルで自動マージ可否を判定する\n- command aidd:design-doc: 要件から設計書を生成し docs/design/ に保存する\n- command aidd:design-review: 設計ドキュメントや実装方針を多観点でレビューする\n- command aidd:design-sync: 設計書と実装の乖離を検知し、status を最新化する\n- command aidd:doctor: aidd/superpowers の導入状態・バージョン整合・hooks 実行可否を診断する\n- command aidd:eval: design-review パイプラインをゴールデンセットで評価し、検出率・誤棄却率を測定する\n- command aidd:incident-retro: セッションで起きた事故を棚卸しし、再発防止の置き場 (コード・hook・CLAUDE.md・memory・コマンド・ADR・issue) を決めて定着させる\n- command aidd:infra-audit: 利用側プロジェクトの静的解析(複雑度制御)・重複コード検出・多OS CI導入状況を診断する\n- command aidd:issue-implement: issue 1本を着手判断から完了報告まで進める入口。実装の中身は superpowers と aidd の既存資産に委ねる\n- command aidd:issue-select: open issue から今着手できる分を選び、提案で止める\n- command aidd:issue-split: 設計を独立マージ可能なPR単位に分割し、GitHub issue 化する\n- command aidd:retro: aidd 資産の棚卸し。利用実績と陳腐化した資産を洗い出す\n- command aidd:test-perspectives: 実装対象・変更差分からテスト観点を洗い出す\n- skill aidd:adr-recall: Use when making an architectural decision, changing existing structure, or proposing a design that could contradict a past decision. Checks docs/adr/ for related ADRs before proceeding.\n- skill aidd:four-kinds-check: Use right before git commit when the staged diff adds code comments or test names, or when drafting the commit message, in a project whose CLAUDE.md has the How / What / Why / Why-not comment placement rule or where AIDD_COMMIT_WHY_CANON is set. Not for reviewing someone else's existing code.\n- skill aidd:issue-priority: Use when asked to set, review, or triage the priority label of GitHub issues, or when about to file a GitHub issue (gh issue create) in a repository that uses priority labels (AIDD_REQUIRED_LABEL_PREFIX is set, .aidd/issue-priority.md exists, or gh label list shows priority labels). Not for ordering implementation tasks inside a plan.\n- skill aidd:model-selection: Use when dispatching a subagent, choosing a model parameter (haiku/sonnet/opus/fable), or unsure whether a task is cheap enough for a smaller model.\n- skill aidd:parallel-coordinator: Use when acting as the coordinator that has multiple workers implement several issues or tasks in parallel.\n- skill aidd:review-loop: Use when running repeated review-fix rounds (design review, PR review, or subagent findings) and deciding when to stop, or when findings arrive in mixed severity vocabularies.\n- agent aidd:design-arbiter: Final arbiter for design reviews. Use after parallel reviewer agents return their findings, to resolve contradictions and pick the single highest-priority fix. Requires deep judgment, so it always runs on opus regardless of the main-loop model.\n- agent aidd:refuter: Adversarial verifier for review findings. Use after reviewer agents return high/mid findings, to actively attempt to refute each finding against the actual target before it is accepted. Findings that survive refutation are promoted; refuted ones are discarded with reasons.\n- agent aidd:reviewer: Code and document reviewer for routine quality checks. Use after a task completes to verify the deliverable matches its requirements. For deep architectural review use the design-review command instead.\n- agent aidd:scout: Lightweight read-only investigator. Use for codebase reconnaissance, file inventories, and fact-finding that only needs conclusions, not analysis. Dispatch multiple scouts in parallel for independent questions.\n- agent aidd:security-reviewer: STRIDE-based threat reviewer for designs that cross trust boundaries (external input, authn/authz, secrets, public endpoints). Launched conditionally by design-review; also usable standalone on a design document.\n- agent aidd:source-verifier: Verifies externally checkable claims in a design document (tech choices, API/spec assertions, version compatibility) against official docs and specs. Opt-in via design-review's --verify-sources flag.\n- hook aidd:session-start: [SessionStart] SessionStart hook: surface aidd assets so they are used without relying on memory.\n- hook aidd:tool-reminder: [PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, PreToolUse] Event-aware Bash hook dispatcher (PreToolUse + PostToolUse). Every check runs in this one\n- hook aidd:usage-log: [PreToolUse, UserPromptSubmit] UserPromptSubmit + PreToolUse(Skill) hook: log aidd command usage for /aidd:retro.\n- hook aidd:write-guard: [PreToolUse] Write/Edit/NotebookEdit guard for new files: unreadable names, and assets aidd (or a listed plugin) already has.\n\nIf it overlaps, respond {\"ok\": false, \"reason\": \"<the aidd asset to use instead, and: if it falls short, file a request against aidd rather than creating a local copy>\"}. If it does not overlap, respond {\"ok\": true}.",
            "continueOnBlock": true
          },
